BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bristol Art Museum Announces Call for Art: Light in Motion
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTSTAMP:20260831T174237Z
UID:2f7fed4ae06641602059d0e807af@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:The Bristol Art Museum invites artists to submit original work
 s for Light in Motion\, an upcoming exhibition exploring the dynamic relat
 ionship between light\, movement\, and artistic expression. The exhibition
  will be on view at the Bristol Art Museum’s community gallery at Rogers
  Free Library from Tues. Sept. 29 through Wed.\, Nov. 18. The deadline for
  submissions is Mon.\, Aug 31. Light has long been one of the most powerfu
 l forces in art\, capable of transforming mood\, perspective\, and experie
 nce. Artists are invited to interpret the many ways light shapes the world
  around us\, from the changing qualities of light across seasons and place
 s\, to the interplay of shadows\, reflections\, and illumination. Submitte
 d works may explore fleeting moments\, shifting rhythms\, movement\, or th
 e symbolic connections between light\, transformation\, and discovery. “
 Light in Motion invites artists to capture not only what we see\, but also
  what we feel\,” said Jennifer Tappero\, Bristol Art Museum at the Roger
 s Free Library Committee member. “We look forward to showcasing works th
 at reveal the many ways artists use light and movement to tell stories\, e
 voke emotions\, and offer new perspectives on the world around us.” The 
 exhibition will be juried by Greg Anthony\, an award-winning photographer 
 whose creative studio career spans more than 40 years. Formerly based in B
 oston\, Anthony now resides in Bristol\, where he has focused on his fine 
 art photography and connecting with art collectors. His commercial work ha
 s included creative studio and location imagery for clients ranging from F
 ortune 500 companies to emerging businesses. Known for vibrant\, detailed 
 images that highlight the complexity of his subjects\, Anthony brings exte
 nsive experience and a unique artistic perspective to the selection proces
 s. Artists age 18 and older are invited to submit original\, ready-to-inst
 all artwork in the following media: drawing\, painting\, printmaking\, col
 lage\, fiber arts\, and photography. No three-dimensional works will be ac
 cepted. Artwork must not exceed 18” x 24” and may be available for sal
 e. All sales are negotiated directly between the artist and collector\; th
 e Bristol Art Museum does not take commissions. Additional information can
  be found at http://www.bristolartmuseum.org/light-in-motion.html\n\nSourc
 e: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/bristol-art-museum-announces-cal
 l-for-art%3a-light-in-motion/111312/
LOCATION:Bristol Art Museum\, 10 Wardwell Street\, Bristol\, 02908
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/bristol-art-museum-announces-ca
 ll-for-art%3a-light-in-motion/111312/
END:VEVENT
